## Interface sketches

```text
slice:            benchmark (existing harness) + NEW SLICE benchmark/external/, benchmark/judge/, benchmark/evolve/
spine step:       workflow (run.py cell loop) + infra (native checkout and env builder, baseline store)
public interface: external.ExternalTask(Task).prepare() / check_correctness()  (F-1)
public interface: external.featurebench.load(instance_id, data_rev) / external.swebench_ml.load(instance_id, data_rev) -> ExternalTask  (F-1)
public interface: external.grade.grade(task, candidate_tree) -> GradeReport(resolved, pass_rate, f2p, p2p)  (F-1)
public interface: external.preflight.admit(instance_id) -> PreflightVerdict  (F-1)
public interface: baselines.run_key(cell) -> str; baselines.lookup(key) -> Row | None; baselines.store(row)  (F-3)
public interface: run.py --panel PATH --max-usd FLOAT --cell-estimate-usd FLOAT --candidate-sha SHA  (F-6, F-2)
public interface: panels.load_panel(path) -> Panel(dev, test)  (F-1)
public interface: judge.applicability(task) -> Label; judge.critique(row, trajectory) -> str; judge.calibrate(labels) -> Agreement  (F-5)
public interface: evolve.main(--panel, --max-usd, --max-metric-calls, --seed-sha); evolve.materialize(candidate) -> sha; evolve.cascade(sha) -> (score, side_info); evolve.finish(frontier)  (F-2, F-3, F-4)
private:          uv venv build from repo_settings; Go/Rust test-output parsers; masked-state reconstruction; trajectory sidecar format; judge prompts; GEPA engine config; mutation allowlist; AGENTS.md regen and byte-lock rewrite; quota classifier
crust delta:      new run.py flags (--panel, --max-usd, --cell-estimate-usd, --candidate-sha); new row fields (run_key, task_digest, env_fingerprint, cli_version, timeout_s, trajectory_path, pass_rate, contaminated); new packages external/judge/evolve; PHASE4_PLAN.md superseded
arrows:           run.py -> external, baselines, panels; evolve -> run.py, baselines, judge, panels; judge -> baselines (row and sidecar read); no arrow from tilth src/ into benchmark/
```

## Risks

- Masked-state reconstruction by reverse-applying the gold patch is [speculating]; AC-3's round trip is the only proof, and tasks that fail it drop out.
- About six of Pareto-12 are expected to build in a local `uv` venv (sympy, metaflow, seaborn ×2, xarray, pydantic) [speculating]; the FeatureBench share of the panel may be small.
- Native execution has no network isolation; an agent can fetch the upstream fix. The contamination flag detects known paths, not every leak.
- Host toolchain drift changes results; the env fingerprint invalidates frozen baselines rather than mixing them.
- Anthropic's Consumer Terms bar automated access except via an API key "or where we otherwise explicitly permit it", while Anthropic documents `setup-token` for scripts; the exposure falls on the maintainer's account.
- Subscription quota (5-hour and weekly windows) bounds throughput; long runs will stop and resume.
- Per-instance Pareto selection chases noise on expensive rollouts; frontier re-runs cost extra budget.
- Mutating `src/` invites overfitting to a small dev split; `just check` and the held-out test split are the guards.
- Retiring the power gate removes the statistical stop; `--max-usd` limits effort but not false-positive conclusions.

## Open questions

- [TBD] Judge agreement threshold and calibration-set size (default proposal: every panel task for applicability plus 20 trajectories, Cohen's kappa ≥ 0.6).
- [TBD] Frontier re-run count and plateau window (default proposal: 3 re-runs; stop after 5 rounds without dev improvement).

## Quality gates

- `just check`: exits 0 (fmt, clippy, cargo test, `tests/mcp_v2`, `tests/scripts`, bash-guard self-test).
- `cd benchmark && python3 -m pytest tests`: exits 0, including the new `test_external.py`, `test_panels.py`, `test_baselines.py`, `test_judge.py`, `test_evolve.py`, `test_analyze.py`.
- `python3 benchmark/external/preflight.py --panel benchmark/panels/<name>.json`: every admitted task reports gold resolved, empty and tampered unresolved.

